  <div class="faq-heading" data-reveal="">
  <p class="eyebrow">Frequently asked questions</p>
  <h2 class="section-title">Clear answers before you commit.</h2>
  <p class="section-copy">Still unsure whether this is the right starting point? We will review the actual client opportunity before recommending a build.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-list" data-reveal="">
  <details class="faq-item"><summary>How quickly can a company store be launched?</summary><p>A straightforward store can often be launched within a few weeks after products, branding, content, and fulfillment requirements are confirmed. Custom functionality may extend the timeline.</p></details>
  <details class="faq-item"><summary>Do we need to carry inventory?</summary><p>No. A company store can launch with print on demand and no upfront inventory. It can also use pre produced inventory for faster delivery and better unit economics, or a hybrid model that stocks core products while producing the rest after the order.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Is Company Store Launch only a print on demand store?</summary><p>No. Print on demand is one fulfillment option, not the identity of the service. We can configure a company store around print on demand, stocked inventory, or a practical hybrid model based on the client program.</p></details>
  <details class="faq-item"><summary>Can the store use the client’s branding?</summary><p>Yes. The storefront can be designed around the client’s approved colors, logo, products, and visual guidelines.</p></details>
  <details class="faq-item"><summary>Who owns the Shopify store?</summary><p>Store ownership and account structure are agreed before development. We recommend keeping the account under the distributor’s or client’s control, depending on the business arrangement.</p></details>
  <details class="faq-item"><summary>Can we add more products later?</summary><p>Yes. Your team can manage products after launch, or Swishtag can provide ongoing support.</p></details>
  <details class="faq-item"><summary>Can this connect with SAGE?</summary><p>SAGE integration is available through the separate SAGE Powered Company Store solution. It requires workflow discovery and a defined integration scope.</p></details>
  <details class="faq-item"><summary>Can the store support multiple clients?</summary><p>This package is designed around one company store. Distributors managing multiple stores may need Enterprise Company Store Automation.</p></details>
  <details class="faq-item"><summary>Does the package include Shopify fees?</summary><p>No. Shopify subscriptions, paid applications, domain costs, transaction fees, product production, inventory, storage, shipping, and other third party costs are separate unless explicitly included in the proposal.</p></details>
  <details class="faq-item"><summary>Why use Shopify for a company store?</summary><p>Shopify is a strong fit when the client needs a more branded buying experience, mobile-friendly ordering, flexible fulfillment, custom functionality, or room to add integrations as the program grows. For a simple temporary store, a standard promotional products store platform may be more practical.</p></details><details class="faq-item"><summary>Do we need to replace SAGE, commonsku, ESP+, or our current workflow?</summary><p>No. Shopify can operate as the client-facing commerce layer while your existing back-office process remains in place. Where appropriate, Swishtag can define a separate integration or automation scope rather than forcing a full system replacement.</p></details></div>
  </div>
